ak=Table(ak,ak,ak,aj,"Curriculum","Built around NCERT and a structured, concept-based syllabus; it is widely aligned with Indian competitive exams such as JEE, NEET, CUET.[1][3]","A broader, content-rich syllabus with strong language depth and separate treatment of subjects such as History/Civics Geography from middle school onward.","-based, concept-led, and interdisciplinary with programmes such as MYP and DP designed around global-minded learning.[4]")
aj=Table(aj,ak,ak,aj,"Assessment","CBSE","CISCE","IB","Uses a mix of internal and external; MYP external is optional and DP adds essays, projects, and other coursework-heavy elements.[7]")
aj=Table(aj,ak,aj,"Subject flexibility","CBSE","CISCE","IB","Moderate flexibility but still more fixed than IB","Greater flexibility, especially in subject choice and in how learners connect disciplines.")
aj=Table(aj,ak,aj,"Transferability","CBSE","CISCE","IB","Best when moving between international schools; recognition is global, but local can depend on school level and subject mapping","Transfers best within CISCE schools, but the smaller network can make moves less convenient than CBSE","Transfers most cleanly between CBSE schools within India; CBSE also has the broadest domestic footprint.")
